      "text": "To solve the problem \\(\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{2}{5} \\cdot \\frac{3}{6} \\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\cdots \\frac{49}{52} \\cdot \\frac{50}{53}\\), we start by combining the fractions in a more manageable form.\n\nFirst, recognize that:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{5} = \\frac{2}{1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4} = \\frac{2 \\cdot 1}{4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{6} = \\frac{3}{1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4} = \\frac{3 \\cdot 3}{4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{4}{7} = \\frac{4}{1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4} = \\frac{4 \\cdot 4}{4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3}\n\\]\nand so on. Continue this pattern through \\(\\frac{49}{52}\\) and \\(\\frac{50}{53}\\).\nObserving the pattern, every term \\(\\frac{k}{k+1}\\) can be written as a single term \\(\\frac{k \\cdot k}{k \\cdot (k+1)}\\) or equivalently \\(\\frac{k^2}{(k+1)(k+2)}\\).\n\nThus combining into one fraction simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{2}{5} \\cdot \\frac{3}{6} \\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\cdots \\frac{49}{52} \\cdot \\frac{50}{53} = \\frac{1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdots 49 \\cdot 50}{4 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 7 \\cdots 52 \\cdot 53}\n\\]\n\nEach term simplifies in pairs as:\n\\[\n\\frac{n}{n + 1} = \\frac{n \\cdot n}{n + 1 \\cdot (n + 2)}\n\\]\nThe product can thus be written as:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{4}{5} \\cdots \\frac{48}{49} \\cdot \\frac{49}{50} \\cdot \\frac{50}{51} \\cdot \\frac{51}{52} \\cdot \\frac{52}{53}\n\\]\n\nIn each pair of fractions, we can simplify:\n\\[\n\\frac{n}{n + 1} \\cdot \\frac{n + 1}{n + 2} = \\frac{n}{n + 2}\n\\]\n\nThus all paired fractions simplify as:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{4}{5} \\cdot \\cdots \\cdot \\frac{48}{49} \\cdot \\frac{49}{50} \\cdot \\frac{50}{51} \\cdot \\frac{51}{52} \\cdot \\frac{52}{53}\n\\]\n\nAfter pair integration, all middle fractions cancel out so that the product reduces to just \\(\\frac{1}{53}\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{53}}\\).",
